# nr-office-author-receipt: what the lead applies (every item is in a file this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-author/src/lib.rs
Add, in the module list right after `pub mod page;` (before `pub mod pptx_writer;`):

    pub mod receipt;

and extend the crate doc sentence that lists the modules with: "the composition receipt (`receipt`: what each saved
slide carries, the deck read against its brief, the rendered air joined to it, and what a session has already been
sent)". Nothing else in lib.rs changes.

## 2. native/core/Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, mixdog-workspace-hack
Nothing. `receipt.rs` uses only dependencies the crate already declares (mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base,
mixdog-office-design, mixdog-office-quality, mixdog-ooxml, serde_json); the twin test uses mixdog-office-base with
`test-support` (already a dev-dependency) and mixdog-office-quality. No new edge.

## 3. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` once the wave is merged: it adds the row
of the new set `office-receipt` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-receipt.mjs, 1 file,
golden.json). The set's own MANIFEST.json is already written (native/core/fixtures/office-receipt/MANIFEST.json).

## 4. SERVICE_PENDING (mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs)
Nothing: this task registers no protocol method.

## 5. Consumers (later tasks of the track, not this one)
The engine's session (the task that implements the `review_artifacts::Receipts` trait) calls, in this order:
`receipt::composition_receipt(&snapshot, Some(&brief))` for `Receipts::composition_receipt`;
`mixdog_office_quality::render_air::rendered_air_by_page(images)` mapped with `PageRead::from(&air)` into
`receipt::attach_rendered_air(&mut receipt, &reads)` for `Receipts::attach_rendered_air`; and
`receipt::receipt_for_delivery(&receipt, Some(&mut session.delivered_receipt))` for `Receipts::for_delivery`, with a
`receipt::DeliveredReceipt` held in the session (Node's `session.deliveredReceipt`; a new session starts with
`DeliveredReceipt::default()`). The author call also keeps the receipt it computed (`frameReceipt` of a PDF's working
deck) as a plain `serde_json::Value`.
